    "id": 14,
    "title": "Crawler revamp, Phase 1: close the exposure",
    "why": "Some public results skipped the rules on protected places, tribal nations' land and confidential addresses (review A1-A4). 'Named on pages we read' now gets the listings' guards: a sacred, burial or archaeological place shows only when it's plainly open to visitors; on a nation's land only businesses show, with the nation's name; a shelter's address is never shown; a name that reads as a person's is held. Held places are kept and marked (source_facts.held), never deleted, and never staged as finds. The protected-place check always knows the nations' peoples, and heritage facts tiered before that are re-tiered by the heritage tick. The OpenStreetMap layer gets the nations check (a trailhead or viewpoint on a nation's land waits for the nation; a business there shows with its rules). Guides follow decisions/0133's levels: a place a nation closed, our team hid, or a person held is never named; a place only a public source names is named as plain text, never the way in.",
    "proposals": "handoffs/crawler-revamp.md Phase 1, research/crawler-review-2026-11-13.md A1, A2, A3, A4",
